["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Your bullet drops a hand's width by 200 m and a forearm by 300 m. A 20 km/h wind moves it a hand's width at 200 m. Know the numbers or stay inside 150 m.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of bullet drop for a .308 150 grain load with a 100 metre zero: zero at 100 m, 4 cm low at 150 m, 12 cm at 200 m, about a hand, 27 cm at 250 m and 47 cm at 300 m, about a forearm. A 20 cm band shows the deer vital zone around the crosshair: past 200 m the bullet falls out of it.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m zero, 150 gr: how far it drops</text>\n<rect x=\"78\" y=\"66.0\" width=\"316\" height=\"68.0\" fill=\"#fde3d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"196\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#fde3d3\" stroke=\"#e8a27c\"/><text x=\"44\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">deer vitals</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">20 cm</text>\n<line x1=\"78\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"394\" y2=\"100\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"100\" r=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M27 100 H53 M40 87 V113\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"40\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">crosshair</text>\n<circle cx=\"112\" cy=\"100\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">zero</text>\n<text x=\"112\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text>\n<rect x=\"154\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"13.6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"174\" y=\"132.6\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4 cm</text>\n<text x=\"174\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">150 m</text>\n<rect x=\"216\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"40.8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"159.8\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12 cm</text>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 m</text>\n<rect x=\"278\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"91.8\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"210.8\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">27 cm</text>\n<text x=\"298\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">250 m</text>\n<rect x=\"340\" y=\"100\" width=\"40\" height=\"159.8\" fill=\"#b3261e\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"278.8\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">47 cm</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">300 m</text>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"177.8\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a hand</text>\n<text x=\"360\" y=\"296.8\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a forearm</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>100 m zero: 12 cm low at 200 m, 47 cm low at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Wind of 20 km/h: 17 cm at 200 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Inside 300 m, placement is your limit, not energy <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all key points</summary><ul><li>Two common loads with published tables: Federal Power Shok 150 gr (grain) and Federal Fusion 165 gr <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>With a 100 m (109 yd) <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Zero\">Zero</button>, the 150 gr bullet lands about 12 cm low at 200 m and 47 cm low at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>With a 200 m (219 yd) zero it is about 6 cm high at 100 m, 11 cm low at 250 m and 29 cm low at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A 20 km/h full crosswind pushes the 150 gr bullet about 17 cm at 200 m and 40 cm at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The heavier 165 gr Fusion drops the same but drifts about 30% less in wind <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Your 20 inch barrel is roughly 70 to 100 fps (feet per second) slower than the test barrel, about 3% <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Both loads carry over 1,000 ft lb past 300 m. Energy is not your limit inside 300 m. Placement is <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Load</th><th>Bullet</th><th>Speed</th><th>BC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Power Shok 150 gr</td><td>Soft point</td><td>860 m/s</td><td>.313</td></tr><tr><td>Fusion 165 gr</td><td>Bonded</td><td>823 m/s</td><td>.446</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>BC (ballistic coefficient): higher cuts air better, drifts less <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Tables show the shape. Your 200 m target shows the truth (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: full load details and cross check</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Load</th><th>Bullet</th><th>Muzzle velocity</th><th>BC (ballistic coefficient)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Federal Power Shok .308, 150 gr, part 308A</td><td>Jacketed soft point</td><td>2,820 fps (860 m/s)</td><td>.313</td></tr><tr><td>Federal Fusion .308, 165 gr, part F308FS2</td><td>Bonded soft point</td><td>2,700 fps (823 m/s)</td><td>.446</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Both from Federal's own product pages, read directly 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Federal's tables assume sights 1.5 inches (3.8 cm) above the bore <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>BC: how well the bullet cuts air. Higher is flatter and drifts less. The 165 gr Fusion has the better BC <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Cross check: Hornady American Whitetail 150 gr, item 8090, 2,820 fps from a 24 inch test barrel, 200 yd zero: 1.9 in high at 100 yd, 8.4 in low at 300 yd. Same shape as the Federal 150 gr <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Your bullet may differ. These tables tell you the shape of the curve. Your 200 m target tells you the truth (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>150 gr</th><th>165 gr</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 m (109 yd)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>150 m (164 yd)</td><td>4 cm low</td><td>4 cm low</td></tr><tr><td>200 m (219 yd)</td><td>12 cm low</td><td>13 cm low</td></tr><tr><td>250 m (273 yd)</td><td>27 cm low</td><td>27 cm low</td></tr><tr><td>300 m (328 yd)</td><td>47 cm low</td><td>47 cm low</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Hold centre to 150 m. At 200 m, hold on the top third of the vitals (Tip).</li><li>Past 250 m the hold is a guess: do not shoot (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: where these numbers come from</summary><ul><li>Federal publishes drops at 50, 100, 200, 300, 400 and 500 yd. Hunt Mentor fitted a curve through those points and read it off at metric distances. Worst fit error: 0.5 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Direct from Federal, 100 yd zero: 150 gr is 3.9 in low at 200 yd and 14.7 in low at 300 yd. 165 gr is 4.1 in and 14.7 in low <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Hold centre to 150 m. At 200 m hold on the top third of the vitals. Past 250 m the hold is a guess: do not shoot (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 420.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bullet path chart for a .308 with 150 grain Federal Power Shok, factory test barrel, numbers in centimetres, height scale exaggerated. With a 100 metre zero: 0 at 100 m (109 yd), 4 low at 150 m (164 yd), 12 low at 200 m (219 yd), 27 low at 250 m (273 yd), 47 low at 300 m (328 yd). With a 200 metre zero: 6 high at 100 m, 6 high at 150 m, 0 at 200 m, 11 low at 250 m, 29 low at 300 m. Your 20 inch barrel gives a little more drop, so check at 200 m.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"420.0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">.308, 150 gr: 100 m zero vs 200 m zero</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Numbers in cm. Height scale exaggerated.</text>\n<path d=\"M143.0 90 V280.0\" stroke=\"#c9c2ae\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<path d=\"M199.5 90 V280.0\" stroke=\"#c9c2ae\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<path d=\"M256.0 90 V280.0\" stroke=\"#c9c2ae\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<path d=\"M312.5 90 V280.0\" stroke=\"#c9c2ae\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<path d=\"M369.0 90 V280.0\" stroke=\"#c9c2ae\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(26.0 128)\"><path d=\"M-28 -2 H6 V3 H-14 L-20 10 H-28z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"-24\" y=\"-10\" width=\"22\" height=\"5\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n<path d=\"M30.0 120 H377.0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\"/>\n<line x1=\"61.64\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"61.64\" y2=\"106\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<rect x=\"13.2\" y=\"80.0\" width=\"96.9\" height=\"26.0\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/>\n<text x=\"61.64\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Line of sight</text>\n<path d=\"M30.0 132.8 C48.8 130.7 114.8 120.0 143.0 120.0 C171.2 120.0 180.7 126.4 199.5 132.8 C218.3 139.2 237.2 146.1 256.0 158.4 C274.8 170.7 293.7 187.7 312.5 206.4 C331.3 225.1 359.6 259.7 369.0 270.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3.4\"/>\n<path d=\"M30.0 132.8 C48.8 127.5 114.8 106.1 143.0 100.8 C171.2 95.5 180.7 97.6 199.5 100.8 C218.3 104.0 237.2 110.9 256.0 120.0 C274.8 129.1 293.7 139.7 312.5 155.2 C331.3 170.7 359.6 203.2 369.0 212.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"9 5\"/>\n<circle cx=\"143.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"133\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">0</text>\n<circle cx=\"199.5\" cy=\"132.8\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"189.5\" y=\"152.8\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-4</text>\n<circle cx=\"256.0\" cy=\"158.4\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"246\" y=\"178.4\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-12</text>\n<circle cx=\"312.5\" cy=\"206.4\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"302.5\" y=\"226.4\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-27</text>\n<circle cx=\"369.0\" cy=\"270.4\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"359\" y=\"290.4\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-47</text>\n<circle cx=\"143.0\" cy=\"100.8\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"149\" y=\"90.8\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+6</text>\n<circle cx=\"199.5\" cy=\"100.8\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"205.5\" y=\"90.8\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+6</text>\n<circle cx=\"256.0\" cy=\"120.0\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"262\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">0</text>\n<circle cx=\"312.5\" cy=\"155.2\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"318.5\" y=\"145.2\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-11</text>\n<circle cx=\"369.0\" cy=\"212.8\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"375\" y=\"202.8\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">-29</text>\n<text x=\"143\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text>\n<text x=\"143\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">109 yd</text>\n<text x=\"199.5\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">150 m</text>\n<text x=\"199.5\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">164 yd</text>\n<text x=\"256\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 m</text>\n<text x=\"256\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">219 yd</text>\n<text x=\"312.5\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">250 m</text>\n<text x=\"312.5\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">273 yd</text>\n<text x=\"369\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">300 m</text>\n<text x=\"369\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b5b4b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">328 yd</text>\n<path d=\"M30 358.0 H70\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3.4\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"363\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">100 m zero</text>\n<path d=\"M210 358.0 H250\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-dasharray=\"9 5\"/><text x=\"258\" y=\"363\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">200 m zero</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"388\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Federal Power Shok 150 gr, factory test barrel.</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"408\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your 20 inch barrel: a little more drop. Check at 200 m.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>About 6 cm high at 100 m, 29 cm low at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Inside 150 m on a small animal, aim low on the chest (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 200 m zero table</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>150 gr Power Shok</th><th>165 gr Fusion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 m (109 yd)</td><td>6 cm high</td><td>7 cm high</td></tr><tr><td>150 m (164 yd)</td><td>6 cm high</td><td>6 cm high</td></tr><tr><td>200 m (219 yd)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>250 m (273 yd)</td><td>11 cm low</td><td>11 cm low</td></tr><tr><td>300 m (328 yd)</td><td>29 cm low</td><td>27 cm low</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Direct from Federal, 200 yd zero: 150 gr is 2.0 in high at 100 yd and 8.8 in low at 300 yd. 165 gr is 2.0 in high and 8.6 in low <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>The bullet never leaves a 15 cm (6 in) band around the crosshair out to about 230 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Cost: on a close shot at a small animal you are 6 cm high. Aim low on the chest inside 150 m (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation from above: wind blows across the shot. The bullet path bends with the wind: 4 cm off at 100 m, 17 cm at 200 m, 40 cm at 300 m. At 300 m it misses the 20 cm vital zone completely.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">20 km/h crosswind, 150 gr bullet</text><g opacity=\".8\"><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"90.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M86.1 71.9 L90.0 80.0 L93.9 71.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 14;0 0\" dur=\"1.6s\" begin=\"0.0s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><g opacity=\".8\"><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M196.1 71.9 L200.0 80.0 L203.9 71.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 14;0 0\" dur=\"1.6s\" begin=\"0.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><g opacity=\".8\"><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"310.0\" y2=\"80.0\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M306.1 71.9 L310.0 80.0 L313.9 71.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 14;0 0\" dur=\"1.6s\" begin=\"0.8s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">wind</text><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"125\" y=\"130\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">100 m</text><rect x=\"235\" y=\"130\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">200 m</text><rect x=\"345\" y=\"130\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".3\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">300 m</text><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/><path id=\"sk-wind-drift-p\" d=\"M46 150 C60.0 151.3, 97.7 152.3, 130.0 158.0 C162.3 163.7, 203.3 172.0, 240.0 184.0 C276.7 196.0, 331.7 222.3, 350.0 230.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 5\"/><circle r=\"6\" fill=\"#23261f\"><animateMotion dur=\"3s\" begin=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\" calcMode=\"linear\"><mpath href=\"#sk-wind-drift-p\"/></animateMotion></circle><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.3s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"158\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">4 cm</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"184\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">17 cm</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.5s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"230\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#b3261e\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">40 cm</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.2s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Past 200 m it blows out of the vitals</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>A 20 km/h crosswind pushes the bullet off the vitals. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Drift grows fast: double the distance, 4 times the drift <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Wind at 45 degrees: use about 70% of the table <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the wind drift table and how to judge wind</summary><p>Full crosswind, blowing straight across the shot, in cm.</p><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>150 gr, 10 km/h</th><th>150 gr, 20 km/h</th><th>165 gr, 10 km/h</th><th>165 gr, 20 km/h</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>100 m (109 yd)</td><td>2</td><td>4</td><td>1.5</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>150 m (164 yd)</td><td>5</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td>6.5</td></tr><tr><td>200 m (219 yd)</td><td>8</td><td>17</td><td>6</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>250 m (273 yd)</td><td>13</td><td>27</td><td>10</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>300 m (328 yd)</td><td>20</td><td>40</td><td>14</td><td>28</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Federal lists drift for a 10 mph (16 km/h) crosswind: 150 gr 4.4 in at 200 yd, 10.4 in at 300 yd. 165 gr 3.1 in and 7.5 in <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Drift grows in a straight line with wind speed, so Hunt Mentor scaled to 10 and 20 km/h and read off metric distances <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>10 km/h: you feel it on your face, leaves rustle. 20 km/h: small branches move, dust lifts <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Wind at 45 degrees: use about 70% of the table <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Wind from the front or behind: ignore at these ranges (Tip).</li><li>Doubling the distance from 150 m to 300 m makes the drift 4 times bigger <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>No shot past 200 m in a real wind this season. Inside 150 m, hold centre and forget the wind.</p></aside>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Barrel</th><th>150 gr speed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>24 inch (test)</td><td>843 m/s (2,766 fps)</td></tr><tr><td>20 inch (yours)</td><td>817 m/s (2,679 fps)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>About 3% slower than the box says <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>About 1 cm more drop at 200 m, 3 cm at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Only your own 200 m group knows the real number (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the barrel test in detail</summary><ul><li>Rifleshooter.com cut a .308 barrel from 28 to 16.5 inches, one inch at a time, and chronographed four loads at each length <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>24 inch versus 20 inch: a 150 gr load went 2,766 to 2,679 fps (87 fps slower). A 168 gr load 2,635 to 2,565 fps (70 fps). A 180 gr load 2,553 to 2,478 fps (75 fps) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Average loss across the whole test: 21 to 25 fps per inch of barrel, depending on the load <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The Berger reloading manual says about 20 fps per inch from a 24 inch barrel, as quoted in that test <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>So expect roughly 80 to 100 fps less than the box says. About 3% <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Effect: about 1 cm more drop at 200 m and about 3 cm more at 300 m, a touch more wind drift. Hunt Mentor estimate: drop grows with the square of the speed loss <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Only a chronograph or your own 200 m group knows your real number. Shoot the group (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 353.0\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Maximum point blank range, MPBR, drawn as a 20 cm pipe the size of deer vitals. For a 150 grain bullet the path rises to 9 cm high at 100 m, crosses the crosshair at the 230 m zero and leaves the bottom of the pipe at about 270 m. Inside that, hold dead centre, no hold over.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"353.0\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Point blank range: the pipe idea</text>\n<rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"110.0\" width=\"336.0\" height=\"80.0\" fill=\"#fde3d3\"/>\n<path d=\"M30.0 110.0 H366.0 M30.0 190.0 H366.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"7 4\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"366.0\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"40.0\" fill=\"#f9cdb2\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"40.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"366.0\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n<path d=\"M30.0 165.2 C39.3 159.2 67.3 137.7 86.0 129.2 C104.7 120.7 124.8 117.2 142.0 114.0 C159.2 110.8 173.2 108.8 189.0 110.0 C204.9 111.2 220.8 114.5 237.2 121.2 C253.6 127.9 271.7 138.5 287.6 150.0 C303.5 161.5 320.1 178.3 332.4 190.0 C344.7 201.7 356.7 215.0 361.5 220.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<circle cx=\"142.0\" cy=\"114.0\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<circle cx=\"287.6\" cy=\"150\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<circle cx=\"332.4\" cy=\"190.0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"32\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c2410c\">20 cm pipe (deer vitals)</text>\n<text x=\"142\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" stroke=\"#fde3d3\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">9 cm high</text>\n<text x=\"283.12\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\" stroke=\"#fde3d3\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">zero 230 m</text>\n<text x=\"70.32\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fde3d3\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">crosshair</text>\n<line x1=\"332.4\" y1=\"196.0\" x2=\"332.4\" y2=\"212.0\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n<text x=\"332.4\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">MPBR 270 m</text>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"256.0\" x2=\"366.0\" y2=\"256.0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"256.0\" x2=\"30.0\" y2=\"262.0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"30\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">0 m</text>\n<line x1=\"142.0\" y1=\"256.0\" x2=\"142.0\" y2=\"262.0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"142\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text>\n<line x1=\"254.0\" y1=\"256.0\" x2=\"254.0\" y2=\"262.0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"254\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 m</text>\n<line x1=\"366.0\" y1=\"256.0\" x2=\"366.0\" y2=\"262.0\" stroke=\"#6b5b4b\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n<text x=\"366\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">300 m</text>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"290.0\" width=\"384\" height=\"57\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"313.6\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">150 gr, 20 cm zone.</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"334.6\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hold centre, no hold over</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>MPBR (maximum point blank range): hold centre, still hit the vitals, no hold over <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>150 gr, 20 cm zone: about 270 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: MPBR numbers</summary><ul><li>MPBR (maximum point blank range): the farthest distance where you can hold on the centre of the vitals and still hit inside the vital zone, with no hold over <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Picture a long pipe as wide as the vital zone. Set the zero so the bullet just misses the top of the pipe. Where it hits the bottom is your MPBR <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Deer hunters often use a 20 cm (8 in) circle. Cautious hunters use 15 cm (6 in) <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>150 gr, 15 cm zone: zero at about 210 m, bullet 7 cm high at 100 m, MPBR about 245 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>150 gr, 20 cm zone: zero at about 230 m, 9 cm high at 100 m, MPBR about 270 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The 165 gr numbers are within 5 m of those <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Real world: rifle error, shooter wobble, altitude and wind all eat into MPBR. Spomer advises using a smaller zone than the real vitals <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Zero at 100 m this season, as the sighting in session says. MPBR is a tool for after you pass the 250 m range test. A 9 cm high bullet at 100 m is a bad trade for a beginner in timber.</p></aside></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>150 gr</th><th>165 gr</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Muzzle</td><td>3,590 J</td><td>3,620 J</td></tr><tr><td>100 m</td><td>2,840 J</td><td>3,060 J</td></tr><tr><td>200 m</td><td>2,210 J</td><td>2,570 J</td></tr><tr><td>300 m</td><td>1,700 J</td><td>2,140 J</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Rule of thumb: 1,000 ft lb (1,356 J) for deer. Both loads pass at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A good bullet through both lungs matters more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: energy in ft lb, the rule and expansion</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Distance</th><th>150 gr Power Shok</th><th>165 gr Fusion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Muzzle</td><td>2,648 ft lb (3,590 J)</td><td>2,671 ft lb (3,620 J)</td></tr><tr><td>100 m (109 yd)</td><td>2,090 ft lb (2,840 J)</td><td>2,260 ft lb (3,060 J)</td></tr><tr><td>200 m (219 yd)</td><td>1,630 ft lb (2,210 J)</td><td>1,900 ft lb (2,570 J)</td></tr><tr><td>300 m (328 yd)</td><td>1,250 ft lb (1,700 J)</td><td>1,580 ft lb (2,140 J)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Muzzle energy direct from Federal. Metric distances read from a curve through Federal's velocities <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Direct from Federal at 300 yd: 150 gr 1,341 ft lb, 165 gr 1,660 ft lb <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rule of thumb:</strong> \"1,000 ft lb (1,356 J) at the animal for deer\". Often credited to Townsend Whelen. Writer Richard Mann calls it an urban legend with no clear origin <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>By that rule both loads are fine past 300 m. It is not your limit <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Federal lists a minimum velocity of 1,900 fps for Fusion to expand. The 165 gr is still above 1,900 fps at 400 yd (366 m) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Power Shok minimum: not listed, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>What matters more: a bullet built for the job, put through both lungs <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Trusting the box table</td><td>Shoot your own 200 m group</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting the wind</td><td>Read the wind table first</td></tr><tr><td>200 m zero, shot over the back at 120 m</td><td>Aim low inside 150 m</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>The bullet knows the wind and the distance. You have to know them first.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Tape inside the scope cap: \"100 m zero. 200 m: 12 low. 250 m: 27 low. Wind 20 km/h at 200 m: 17.\" Read it before every stalk.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: 3 common mistakes</summary><ul><li>Memorising a drop table from the box, never shooting at 200 m to check it.</li><li>Forgetting the wind. Drop is easy to see on paper, drift is not.</li><li>Using a 200 m zero and shooting over a deer's back at 120 m.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Federal and Hornady tables 85%. Barrel test, MPBR and energy notes 65 to 75%. Checked 2026-10-01.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.federalpremium.com/rifle/power-shok/11-308A.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Federal Power Shok .308 Win 150 gr, part 308A, ballistics tab</a>, velocity, energy, wind drift at 10 mph, drops for 100 yd and 200 yd zero, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.federalpremium.com/rifle/fusion/11-F308FS2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Federal Fusion .308 Win 165 gr, part F308FS2, ballistics tab</a>, same tables, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.hornady.com/ammunition/rifle/308-win-150-gr-interlock-sp-american-whitetail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hornady .308 Win 150 gr InterLock American Whitetail, item 8090</a>, 24 inch test barrel, 200 yd zero table, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://rifleshooter.com/2014/12/308-winchester-7-62x51mm-nato-barrel-length-versus-velocity-28-to-16-5/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rifleshooter.com: .308 barrel length versus velocity, 28 to 16.5 inches</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.americanhunter.org/content/learn-your-maximum-point-blank-range/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Hunter: learn your maximum point blank range, Ron Spomer</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://empty-cases.com/blog/myth-busters-the-1000-foot-pound-fairy-tale/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Richard Mann: the 1000 foot pound fairy tale</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Metric tables, MPBR figures and the 20 inch estimate: computed by Hunt Mentor from the manufacturer points above, 2026-10-01 (65 to 75%). Wind feel cues: Beaufort scale, from memory <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]